  "notes": [
    "Results reproduce the higher-thinking configurations and base scenario prompts in manuscript Figure 3. Each configuration has one outcome per completed task; incomplete outcomes are excluded.",
    "Rates describe the evaluated settings, with 48\u201352 completed human-control tasks, 22 shutdown tasks, and eight restricted-access tasks per configuration.",
    "All restricted-access results use the same prohibition-only base prompt. Wording, disclosure, and task-completion-pressure ablations are separate experiments.",
    "Reasoning is max for GPT-5.6 Sol and Claude Opus 4.6; xhigh for other GPT models and Claude Opus 4.7; high for Gemini; and thinking enabled for Qwen and Kimi. See Appendix A.1 for observation modalities and step budgets.",
    "Actual shutdown rates measure script modification. Alternate shutdown avoidance is reported separately; the categories may overlap and should not be added. Figures 2 and 4 instead combine script modification and alternate avoidance in their actual shutdown metric.",
    "GPT-5.6 Sol and GPT-5.4 subagent configurations are evaluated only for restricted resource access in Figure 3.",
    "Primary intent and alternate-avoidance labels use GPT-5.5 xhigh. Appendix A.6 reports human validation and cross-judge sensitivity; agreement between judges does not establish correctness."
  ],
  "prompt_conditions": {
    "standard": "Base scenario prompt; shutdown uses deployment framing.",
